 """
-Adapted SERSFormer2 core model for fixed 1901-point Raman input.
-
-The original SERSFormer2 architecture is retained conceptually:
-- classification CNN -> shared Transformer encoder -> classification MLP
-- smoothed-signal CNN -> shared Transformer encoder
-- percentile-feature CNN + transformer feature fusion -> regression MLP
-
-Engineering adaptations:
-- input length is fixed to 1901 points
-- 1401-point spectra are zero-padded by Dataset.py and accompanied by valid_mask
-- valid_mask is downsampled through the same Conv/Pool geometry
-- Transformer receives src_key_padding_mask
-- invalid output tokens are zeroed before the original flatten+MLP heads
-- hard-coded 172 tokens are replaced by the correct token count for 1901 points
+Peak-guided SERSFormer for the DEL/CHL/TEB multi-task SERS project.
+
+Model path:
+    three 1-D CNN branches
+        raw spectrum / smoothed spectrum / percentile features
+    -> token-level feature fusion
+    -> shared Transformer encoder
+    -> pesticide-specific peak-guided query attention
+    -> one classification head and one concentration head per pesticide
+
+Key design points:
+- DEL, CHL and TEB each own a learnable query vector.
+- Every query can attend to every *valid* Raman token.
+- Training-data-derived peak priors add a positive soft bias to attention logits;
+  they never delete non-peak regions.
+- valid_mask remains authoritative. A short 1401-point spectrum cannot attend to
+  padded 2000-2500 cm^-1 positions even if a pesticide prior has a peak there.
+- The public forward interface remains [classification_probability, concentration].
 """
 
